#{[17592186524933 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524933 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524933 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524933 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524933 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d4cb4e3c-90dc-5a4e-ad03-801bee72ca2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524937 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524937 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524937 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524937 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524937 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dffaf696-90ee-57c0-93f5-481258f07333" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524946 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524946 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524946 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524946 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f068fa89-ce05-5148-b62a-30202a76bdb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524948 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f4cb0872-1c1c-5be2-826b-83e8a8aaf2ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524974 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524974 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524974 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524974 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524974 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31ce7adb-3732-5d9f-92f5-a50363ba4c8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524974 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524976 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524976 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524976 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524976 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x)}{\\sqrt{x}},$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}($ \n{{field-1}} $-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3337e5e0-9e46-58ca-9b60-fe0a52d9614e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524976 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x)$ and $v(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{{[v(x)]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′}}{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′}}{x} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524986 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524986 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341554" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524986 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524986 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x,$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x}{x}\\,-$ \n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "54c54e62-4a18-5ab6-878d-ec4e2ae2aaa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524986 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a product $u(x)\\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡x\\,+\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524988 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341535" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524988 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524988 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2/3}}$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524988 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "585fdeed-02dd-5444-8201-a19fa1a46351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524988 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[3\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-{(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2/3}}\\frac{1}{(1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525000 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525000 #edb/ref 1069 "q-313249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525000 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525000 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)},$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\frac{1}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525000 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b99a120-8ee4-5c4d-80c5-2291fb8275da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525000 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1).$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-(2x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (2x-1)^{′}=\\frac{2}{4x-4{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(4x-4{x}^{2})\\,{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-4{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{1}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525005 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525005 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341522" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525005 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525005 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(1-x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525005 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88d8545b-9874-55b6-990b-870f4aec4ac1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525005 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(1-x)^{2}}\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(1-2x+{x}^{2})}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x(x-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525007 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525007 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95528" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525007 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525007 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8af41eb0-cd12-5003-8c4d-9b2fa7191b55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525007 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^{2}⁡x}})\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^{2}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525015 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525015 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525015 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525015 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}+g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525015 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9939cec3-a9a6-5501-8d65-e82136850623" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525015 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95544" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525019 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{-x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ebac606-d705-5196-a808-5592aaa317af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525019 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{-x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{-x})^{′} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{-2x}}\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}-{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{-2x}}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525026 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525026 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525026 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525026 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=6\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525026 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa97bd1f-f2ce-5f6f-ba26-21c15fc2c29a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525026 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-6\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{1+(3x-1)^{2}}})\\cdot (3x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{1+9{x}^{2}-6x+1}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525033 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525033 #edb/ref 1069 "q-313240" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525033 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525033 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\,\\operatornam